Here is a standard, comprehensive `.gitignore` file tailored for a Go project:

```gitignore
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe-e
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (if using vendor folder without committing it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# IDE & Editor Specific Files
# VS Code
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

# JetBrains / GoLand
.idea/
*.iml

# Sublimetext
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# Operating System Files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Environment variables & local configuration files
.env
.env.local
*.local.json

# Local build artifacts (common bin output directory)
/bin/
/dist/

```